{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "איש אל רעהו הבה", :translit "ish el re'ehu havah", :gloss "each man to his fellow, come"} {:he "שלוה", :translit "shelavah", :gloss "tranquility"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "איש אל רעהו הבה", :spells "שלוה"}], :frame {:text "The end-letters of 'איש אל רעהו הבה' (Genesis 11:3) spell 'שלוה', signaling the sin behind the Tower of Babel. The Ba'al HaTurim reads the verse's own letters as an indictment: their tranquility was the very root of their rebellion. Jeremiah 48:11 pronounces wrath upon Moab 'because he has rested on his lees' (the imagery of undisturbed wine), and the midrash applies this principle universally —安宁 breeding sin, as at Babel.", :sources ["Genesis 11:3" "Jeremiah 48:11"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לאבן", :translit "la'even", :gloss "for stone"} {:he "וימת לבו בקרבו והוא היה לאבן", :translit "va'yamat libo b'qirbo v'hu hayah la'even", :gloss "and his heart died within him and he became like a stone"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["לאבן" "לאבן"]}], :frame {:text "The word לאבן occurs exactly twice in Scripture: at Genesis 11:3 and at 1 Samuel 25:37. At 1 Samuel 25:37 Nabal's heart dies within him and he becomes 'like a stone,' and ten days later the Lord strikes him and he dies (1 Samuel 25:38). The gezeirah shavah linking the two — 'just as there it speaks of death, so too here' — carries the thematic association of לאבן with mortality from the Nabal narrative onto the Tower of Babel narrative.", :sources ["Genesis 11:3" "1 Samuel 25:37" "1 Samuel 25:38"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "איש אל רעהו הבה", :spells "שלוה", :letters ["ש" "ל" "ו" "ה"], :by :selah, :order :in-order} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["לאבן" "לאבן"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "לאבן", :refs ["Genesis 11:3" "1 Samuel 25:37" "Habakkuk 2:19"], :n 3, :lens :exact} {:phrase "לאבן", :refs ["Genesis 11:3" "1 Samuel 25:37" "Habakkuk 2:19"], :n 3, :lens :exact}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:05:20.354098430Z", :model "glm-5.2"}